+// Brain Engine 0014: card sharing between Brain Engine builds on different llama.cpp versions.
+// A graph sent to a lent card names each step by its number in ggml's list of operations (rpc_tensor.op). llama.cpp
+// renumbers that list now and then (1.0 dropped ADD1 and DIAG_MASK_INF/ZERO, so every later step moved down), and
+// upstream then raises RPC_PROTO_MAJOR_VERSION so mismatched builds refuse each other. Brain Engine instead keeps one
+// frozen numbering on the wire, the one card-sharing protocol 9 used (llama.cpp b12282, Brain Engine 7), and says 9
+// in HELLO. Each side turns its own numbers into wire numbers and back, so Brain Engine 7 and every later build share
+// cards both ways. When llama.cpp adds a step, add it at the END of this list (never in the middle); when it drops
+// one, put -1 in its place. A step this build has no number for, or a wire number it doesn't know, is refused with
+// a clear message instead of running the wrong math. Nothing else in the messages differs between protocol 9 and 10.
+#define BOB_WIRE_MAJOR 9
+#define BOB_WIRE_MINOR 0
+#define BOB_WIRE_PATCH 0
+static constexpr int bob_wire_ops[] = {
